Package: splitTypeR
Type: Package
Version: 0.99.9
Date: 2026-10-24
Title: Transcriptomic Classification using Mixture of Normal Distributions
Description: The splitTypeR package enables the classification of bulk 
    transcriptomic samples using gene signature lists. For each 
    signature, an enrichment score is first calculated for every sample with 
    Bioconductor GSVA, and the uncertainty around each score is 
    estimated through permutations of the samples. Values drawn from 
    the sample-specific normal distributions are then pooled to fit 
    a mixture of two normal distributions that represents the whole cohort. 
    Each sample is finally tested against the distribution with the 
    lower mean, and samples with a significantly higher score are assigned 
    to the signature. Published gene signatures related to pancreatic ductal 
    adenocarcinoma subtyping are also provided.
